# `task-board.config.json` Canonical Reference

This is the canonical operator reference named by every configuration refusal.
The file is project-scoped: a repository carries at most its own
`task-board.config.json`. A machine-scoped `./scripts/setup.sh` install never
creates, repairs, reformats, or migrates it. Use
`./scripts/setup.sh --configure-project ...` only when you explicitly intend to
write project configuration, or edit the JSON directly.

The schema snapshot used by drift tests is
[`assets/task-board-config/schema.json`](assets/task-board-config/schema.json).
Complete valid snapshots:

- [local + spawn-policy-v2](assets/task-board-config/local-spawn-policy-v2.json)
- [local + spawn-policy-v3](assets/task-board-config/local-spawn-policy-v3.json)
- [remote + spawn-policy-v2](assets/task-board-config/remote-spawn-policy-v2.json)
- [remote + spawn-policy-v3](assets/task-board-config/remote-spawn-policy-v3.json)

Unknown keys, wrong types, unsupported enum values, conflicting legacy/current
sections, and malformed containers are refused as a whole. Task-board does not
continue using understood siblings, guess defaults for rejected fields, or
offer an automatic fix. Found-value summaries are typed and bounded; secret,
token, password, credential, and key-shaped fields plus credential-like nested
values are redacted before diagnostics are stored or rendered.

## Root sections

| Key | Type | Required | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `mode` | `"local"` or `"remote"` | No | `"local"` | Selects the active project profile. |
| `local` | object or `null` | No | `{"board_dir":".task-board"}` | Local board location. |
| `remote` | object or `null` | For a stored remote profile | None | Shared remote server/board profile. |
| `spawn` | object or `null` | No | Runtime defaults | Root spawn policy; remote mode uses it when `remote.spawn` is absent/null. |
| `features` | object or `null` | No | Built-in feature defaults | Root feature registry; remote mode uses it when `remote.features` is absent/null. |
| `agent_context` | object or `null` | No; compatibility only | None | One-release legacy alternative to `features.agent_context`; never configure both. |
| `session_manager` | object or `null` | No | Built-in Codex continuation defaults | Current Session Manager provider settings. |
| `codex` | object or `null` | No; compatibility only | None | Legacy location for Codex session settings; `session_manager` takes precedence. |
| `version_control` | object or `null` | No | `confirm=false` | Scoped commit acknowledgement policy. |

## Local and remote profiles

| Key | Type | Required | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `local.board_dir` | string path | No | `".task-board"` | Board directory, resolved from the project. |
| `remote.url` | URL string | Yes for stored remote profile | None | Board server URL. |
| `remote.board` | non-empty string | Yes for stored remote profile | None | Remote board ID. |
| `remote.tls_no_verify` | boolean | No | `false` | Disables TLS certificate verification. |
| `remote.spawn` | spawn object or `null` | No | Root `spawn` | Remote-only spawn policy. |
| `remote.features` | features object or `null` | No | Root `features` | Remote-only feature registry. |
| `remote.agent_context` | agent-context object or `null` | No; compatibility only | Root/feature defaults | Legacy remote alternative to `remote.features.agent_context`; never configure both. |

`remote.user` and `remote.token` are not canonical shared-project keys. Select a
user with `task-board switch-user`; store tokens with `task-board login` or use
the explicit `TASK_BOARD_TOKEN` environment override. A stored `remote.token`
refuses every command until it is removed manually. Diagnostics report only
that the credential is present and its shape/length; they never echo its value.

## Spawn policy

| Key | Type | Required | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `spawn.enabled` | boolean | No | `true` | Enables tracked child spawning. |
| `spawn.max_parallel` | positive integer | No | `20` | Per-client concurrent runner limit. |
| `spawn.preferred_agentic_system` | exactly one of `{"exclusive":"provider"}` or `{"mixed":["provider",...]}` | No | Runtime affinity | Allowed/preferred provider set. |
| `spawn.preferred_agent` | provider string | No; compatibility only | None | Legacy single-provider preference; do not combine with `preferred_agentic_system`. |
| `spawn.schedule.windows` | non-empty array | No | No schedule | UTC provider-policy windows. |
| `spawn.schedule.windows[].start_utc` | `"HH:MM"` | Yes in a window | None | Inclusive UTC start. |
| `spawn.schedule.windows[].end_utc` | `"HH:MM"` | Yes in a window | None | Exclusive UTC end; an earlier value crosses midnight. |
| `spawn.schedule.windows[].preferred_agentic_system` | tagged provider union | Yes in a window | None | Replaces the base provider set during the window. |
| `spawn.launch_composition.enabled` | boolean | No | `true` | Enables optional agents-infra MCP composition. |
| `spawn.ceilings.contract_version` | `"spawn-policy-v2"` or `"spawn-policy-v3"` | No | `"spawn-policy-v2"` | Selects one disjoint ceiling schema. |

Every root `spawn.*` key may instead appear under `remote.spawn.*`.

### `spawn-policy-v2`

Each of `spawn.ceilings.codex`, `.claude`, and `.qwen` is optional.

| Provider/role key | Type | Required | Allowed/default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `model` | non-empty model ID string | Provider-specific | No default | Compatibility-snapshot model bound. |
| `model_criterion` | string | When required by the configured bound | `equal`, `less_or_equal`, `greater_or_equal` | Comparison direction. |
| `reasoning_effort` | string | Provider-specific | Codex: `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, `ultra`; Qwen: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`; Claude omits it | Effort bound. |
| `roles.<role>.model` | model ID string | No | Inherits provider | Role override. |
| `roles.<role>.model_criterion` | criterion string | No | Inherits provider | Role override. |
| `roles.<role>.reasoning_effort` | effort string | No | Inherits provider | Role override. |

Role names must be supported task-board roles; `coordinator` canonicalizes to
`orchestrator`.

### `spawn-policy-v3`

Each configured provider uses an explicit allow set; model registry rank/order
does not grant admission.

| Provider/role key | Type | Required | Allowed/default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `allowed_models` | non-empty array of unique model IDs | Yes for provider; optional role replacement | None | Exact admission authority. |
| `resolution_model` | admitted model ID string or `null` in a role | No | No fallback | Exact fallback when adjustment is allowed. |
| `adjustment_confirmation` | string | Yes for provider; optional role override | `required`, `none` | Whether adjusted resolution needs acknowledgement. |
| `reasoning_effort` | string | No | Provider default | Effort bound. |
| `reasoning_effort_criterion` | string | Required with a directional effort bound | `less_or_equal`, `greater_or_equal` | Effort direction. |
| `roles.<role>.*` | same fields | No | Inherit provider field-by-field | Role replacement/override. |

